    '2020': r'''[{"id":"utet_2020_q1","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"संज्ञानात्मक विकास","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा सिद्धान्त संज्ञानात्मक विकास की चार प्रमुख अवस्थाओं का प्रतिपादन करता है?","options_hi":["पियाजे का संज्ञानात्मक विकास का सिद्धान्त।","वायगॉट्स्की का सामाजिक विकास का सिद्धान्त।","कोहलबर्ग का संज्ञानात्मक विकास का सिद्धान्त।","बैन्डूरा का सामाजिक सीखने का सिद्धान्त।"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2020 Q1","years":"2020","q_en":"Which theory proposes the four major stages of cognitive development?","options_en":["Piaget's theory of cognitive development.","Vygotsky's theory of social development.","Kohlberg's theory of cognitive development.","Bandura's theory of social learning."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q2","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"बुद्धि","q_hi":"कौन सी निम्नांकित गतिविधि स्थानिक बुद्धि से सम्बन्धित है?","options_hi":["मौखिक अनुनय","एक जटिल उपकरण को इकट्ठा करना।","परिकल्पना का विकास तथा परीक्षण।","भाँप लेना कि कब विनम्र होना है।"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2020 Q2","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following activities is associated with spatial intelligence?","options_en":["Verbal persuasion","Assembling a complex appliance","Developing and testing hypothesis","Sensing when to be tactful"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q3","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"बुद्धि","q_hi":"मन्द-बुद्धि बालकों हेतु कौन सी अभिप्रेरण प्रविधि अधिक उपयोगी होगी?","options_hi":["पुरस्कार एवं प्रशंसा","दण्ड","निन्दा","चुनौती"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2020 Q3","years":"2020","q_en":"Which motivational technique will be more useful for slow learners?","options_en":["Award & appreciation","Punishment","Condemnation","Challenge"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q4","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"समावेशी शिक्षा","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित विशेषताओं में से कौन सी विशिष्ट (प्रतिभाशाली) बालकों की विशेषता **नहीं** है?","options_hi":["वे अपनी आयु के अधिकांश बच्चों से अधिक जल्दी व स्वतंत्र रूप से सीखते हैं।","उनका शब्दकोश अधिक विकसित होता है तथा उनके पढ़ने व लिखने के कौशल अधिक उन्नत होते हैं।","वे स्वयं को सामान्य उपलब्धि के मानकों से ऊपर नहीं रखते हैं।","वे चुनौतीपूर्ण व कठिन कार्यों में बहुत अभिप्रेरित रहते हैं।"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2020 Q4","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following is not a characteristic of gifted children?","options_en":["They learn more quickly and independently than most students of their own age.","They often have well-developed vocabulary, as well as advanced reading and writing skills.","They do not hold themselves to higher than usual standards of achievement.","They are very motivated, especially on tasks that are challenging or difficult."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q5","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम की प्रकृति","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन शिक्षण कौशलों की विशेषता **नहीं** है?","options_hi":["शिक्षण कौशल शिक्षक क्रियाओं अथवा व्यवहारों से सम्बन्धित होते हैं।","शिक्षण कौशल छात्रों के सीखने में सहायता एवं सुगमता प्रदान करते हैं।","शिक्षण कौशल कक्षा शिक्षण व्यवहार की सभी इकाइयों से सम्बन्धित होते हैं।","शिक्षण कौशल शैक्षिक विशिष्ट उद्देश्यों को प्राप्त करने में सहायक होते हैं।"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2020 Q5","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following is not a special feature of teaching skills?","options_en":["Teaching skills are related to actions or behaviours of teachers.","Teaching skills provide assistance and ease to students in learning.","Teaching skills are related to all units of classroom teaching behaviour.","Teaching skills are helpful in achieving the specific educational objectives."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q6","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"व्यक्तित्व","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा कथन शिक्षण की प्रकृति की सटीक व्याख्या **नहीं** करता है?","options_hi":["शिक्षण एक अंतःक्रिया है।","शिक्षण कला और विज्ञान दोनों ही है।","शिक्षण एक विकासात्मक प्रक्रिया है।","शिक्षण केवल शिक्षक के लिए ही उपयोगी है।"],"ans":3,"source":"UTET 2020 Q6","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following statements does not define the nature of teaching exactly?","options_en":["Teaching is interaction.","Teaching is both an art as well as science.","Teaching is a developmental process.","Teaching is useful for the teacher only."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q7","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"व्यक्तित्व","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन अधिगम को स्पष्ट रूप से परिभाषित करता है?","options_hi":["अधिगम प्रक्रिया तथा परिणाम है।","अधिगम एक सतत् प्रक्रिया है।","अधिगम व्यवहार परिवर्तन की प्रक्रिया है।","उपरोक्त सभी।"],"ans":3,"source":"UTET 2020 Q7","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following statements clearly defines learning?","options_en":["Learning is both process and product.","Learning is a continuous process.","Learning is a process of change in behaviour.","All the above."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q8","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"शिक्षण विधियाँ","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी शिक्षण विधि **नहीं** है?","options_hi":["प्रश्नोत्तर विधि","साक्षात्कार विधि","ब्रेन स्टॉर्मिंग विधि","अन्वेषण विधि"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2020 Q8","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following is not a teaching method?","options_en":["Question-answer method","Interview method","Brain storming method","Discovery method"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q9","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"नीति एवं अधिनियम","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से शिक्षण के सूत्र कौन से हैं?","options_hi":["(1) और (3)","(1) और (4)","(2), (3), (4)","उपरोक्त सभी"],"ans":3,"source":"UTET 2020 Q9","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following are the maxims of teaching?*\n\n1. ज्ञात से अज्ञात की ओर। / From known to unknown.\n2. स्थूल से सूक्ष्म की ओर। / From concrete to abstract.\n3. सरल से जटिल की ओर। / From easy to difficult.\n4. पूर्ण से अंश की ओर। / From whole to part.","options_en":["(1) and (3)","(1) and (4)","(2), (3), (4)","All the above"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q10","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"व्यक्तित्व","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन से कारक व्यक्तित्व को प्रभावित करते हैं?","options_hi":["(i) व (ii)","(i), (ii) व (iii)","(i), (iii), (iv)","(ii), (iv)"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2020 Q10","years":"2020"},{"id":"utet_2020_q11","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"व्यक्तित्व","q_hi":"शिक्षा मनोविज्ञान का ज्ञान एक शिक्षक के लिए आवश्यक है, क्योंकि यह –","options_hi":["नवीन शिक्षण तकनीकियों का ज्ञान प्रदान करता है।","समस्त शैक्षिक समस्याओं का सफलतापूर्वक समाधान करने में सहायता करता है।","मूल्यांकन की नवीन तकनीकियों को सीखने में शिक्षक की सहायता करता है।","शिक्षक को स्वयं को समझने में सहायता करता है।"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2020 Q11","years":"2020","q_en":"The knowledge of Educational Psychology is necessary for a teacher because it –","options_en":["Provides knowledge about new teaching techniques.","Helps to solve all types of educational problems successfully.","Helps the teacher to learn new evaluation techniques.","Helps the teacher to know himself."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q12","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम की प्रकृति","q_hi":"वृद्धि और विकास की प्रक्रियाओं के सन्दर्भ में कौन सी बात सही है?","options_hi":["दोनों प्रक्रियायें प्राकृतिक हैं।","वृद्धि प्राकृतिक प्रक्रिया है तथा विकास में बाह्य कारक की आवश्यकता होती है।","यदि वृद्धि संतोषजनक है तो विकास स्वतः हो जाता है।","दोनों प्रक्रियाएँ बिना बाह्य हस्तक्षेप के साथ-साथ चलती हैं।"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2020 Q12","years":"2020","q_en":"Which of the following is true for the processes of growth and development?","options_en":["Both are natural processes.","Growth is natural while development needs external intervention.","If growth is satisfactory, development follows.","Both the processes go together without any external intervention."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q13","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"व्यक्तित्व","q_hi":"व्यक्तित्व के विकास में विरासत तथा परिवेश की भूमिका के सम्बन्ध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन सी बात सही है?","options_hi":["अच्छी विरासत, बुरे परिवेश की क्षतिपूर्ति कर सकती है।","विरासत तथा परिवेश का योगदान बराबर होता है।","बुरा परिवेश, अच्छी विरासत को दबा सकता है।","अच्छा परिवेश, बुरी विरासत की क्षतिपूर्ति कर सकता है।"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2020 Q13","years":"2020","q_en":"In the context of the role of heredity and environment in personality development, which of the following is true?","options_en":["Good heredity can make up for poor environment.","Heredity and environment have equal contribution.","Poor environment can suppress good heredity.","Good environment can make up for poor heredity."]},{"id":"utet_2020_q14","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम की प्रकृति","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किसने बौद्धिक विकास को आयु से सम्बन्धित बताया है?","options_hi":["जेरोम एस. ब्रूनर","जीन पियाजे","डेविड आसुबेल","हिल्डा ताबा"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2020 Q14","years":"2020","q_en":"Who among the following described the intellectual development as age related development?","options_en":["Jerome S. Bruner","Jean Piaget","David Ausubel","Hilda Taba"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q15","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम की प्रकृति","q_hi":"किसी वयस्क के आक्रामक व्यवहार को देखने मात्र से बच्चे आक्रामकता सीख लेते हैं। यह विचार किसका है?","options_hi":["कैटल","ऑलपोर्ट","डोलार्ड और मिलर","बांदुरा और उसके साथी"],"ans":3,"source":"UTET 2020 Q15","years":"2020","q_en":"Children could learn to be aggressive simply by observing an adult behaving aggressively. This point of view is held by –","options_en":["Cattell","Allport","Dollard and Miller","Bandura and his associates"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q16","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"संज्ञानात्मक विकास","q_hi":"कोहलबर्ग के नैतिक विकास सम्बन्धी सिद्धान्त के अन्तर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन सी उस सिद्धान्त की एक अवस्था **नहीं** है?","options_hi":["संवेदी प्रेरक","प्राक्-रूढ़िगत","रूढ़िगत","पश्च-रूढ़िगत"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2020 Q16","years":"2020","q_en":"Which one of the following is not a stage in Kohlberg's theory of moral development?","options_en":["Sensory-motor","Pre-conventional","Conventional","Post-conventional"]},{"id":"utet_2020_q17","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम सिद्धांत","q_hi":"एक छात्र गणित के प्रश्न करते हुए एक प्रश्न पर अटक गया। कुछ समय सोचने के बाद अचानक उसे युक्ति सूझी तथा स