ing is/are not an air pollutant?","options_en":["X-Ray","CO₂, CO gas","SPM particle","SO₂ gas"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q138","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"लघु हिम युग के लिये उत्तरदायी कारक है —","options_hi":["वृक्षारोपण","ज्वालामुखी धूल","अत्यधिक यातायात वाहन","ध्वनि प्रदूषक"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2021 Q138","years":"2021","q_en":"The factor responsible for the Little Ice Age is —","options_en":["Plantations","Volcanic Dust","Excessive Transport Vehicles","Sound Pollutants"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q139","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"रहीम एक तालाब बनाकर, पानी भरकर उसमें मछलियाँ डालता है, लेकिन तालाब में मछलियाँ जीवित नहीं रह पाती हैं। इसका कारण है —","options_hi":["गहरा तालाब","पानी में घुलित ऑक्सीजन की अनुपस्थिति","पक्का तालाब","उपरोक्त में से कोई नहीं"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2021 Q139","years":"2021","q_en":"Raheem prepares a pond, fills water and then disperses fishes in it, but the fishes do not survive in the pond. Its reason is —","options_en":["Deep Pond","Absence of dissolved oxygen in water","Cemented Pond","None of the above"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q140","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"सुरेश ने खेत में मटर बोने के बाद, उसी खेत में बिना खाद का प्रयोग करके गेहूँ का ज्यादा उत्पादन प्राप्त किया, इसका कारण है —","options_hi":["प्रकाशसंश्लेषण","वाष्पोत्सर्जन","राइजोबियम जीवाणु","श्वसन गुणांक"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q140","years":"2021","q_en":"Suresh produced a greater yield of wheat without the use of fertilizers in the same field where peas were cultivated earlier. Its reason is —","options_en":["Photosynthesis","Transpiration","Rhizobium Bacteria","Respiratory Quotient"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q141","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"कृषि एवं मृदा","q_hi":"मृदा के संबंध में निम्न कथनों पर विचार कीजिये तथा नीचे दिये गये कूटों से सही उत्तर का चयन कीजिए —\n1. मृदा भोजन एवं लकड़ी का मुख्य आधार है।\n2. मृदा एक प्रमुख संसाधन है।\n3. सभी समुदाय एवं उनकी संस्कृतियाँ मृदा पर आधारित होती हैं।","options_hi":["1 एवं 2 सत्य हैं","1 एवं 3 सत्य हैं","2 एवं 3 सत्य हैं","1, 2 एवं 3 सत्य हैं"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2021 Q141","years":"2021","q_en":"Consider the following statements about soil and select the correct answer using the code given below —\n1. Soil is the basic medium for food and timber.\n2. Soil is an important resource.\n3. All communities and their cultures depend on soil.\nCode:","options_en":["1 and 2 are correct","1 and 3 are correct","2 and 3 are correct","1, 2 and 3 are correct"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q142","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"निम्न में से कौन-सा एक पृथ्वी के क्रस्ट का सबसे प्रमुख तत्व है?","options_hi":["एल्यूमिनियम","लोहा","ऑक्सीजन","सिलिकन"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q142","years":"2021","q_en":"Which one of the following is the dominant element of the Earth's crust?","options_en":["Aluminium","Iron","Oxygen","Silicon"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q143","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"वन एवं संसाधन","q_hi":"भारत में निम्न में से किस प्रकार का वनावरण सबसे अधिक पाया जाता है?","options_hi":["उष्णकटिबंधीय नम सदाबहार वन","उष्णकटिबंधीय अर्द्ध सदाबहार वन","उष्णकटिबंधीय नम पर्णपाती वन","शुष्क उष्णकटिबंधीय वन"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q143","years":"2021","q_en":"Which of the following types of forests covers the largest area in India?","options_en":["Tropical Wet Evergreen Forests","Tropical Semi-Evergreen Forests","Tropical Moist Deciduous Forests","Dry Tropical Forests"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q144","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"जैव-विविधता","q_hi":"एक प्रजाति के हमेशा के लिए विलुप्त होने की प्रक्रिया में पहला चरण कौन-सा है?","options_hi":["पारिस्थितिकीय विलोपन","सामूहिक विलोपन","स्थानीय विलोपन","जैविक विलोपन"],"ans":3,"source":"UTET 2021 Q144","years":"2021","q_en":"Which is the first stage in the process of a species becoming irreversibly extinct?","options_en":["Ecological extinction","Mass extinction","Local extinction","Biological extinction"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q145","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन वैश्विक स्तर पर जल के बारे में सत्य है?","options_hi":["प्रतिव्यक्ति उपलब्ध जल पर्याप्त नहीं है।","हम पानी का पुनः प्रयोग नहीं कर सकते।","पानी प्रचुर मात्रा में मौजूद है किन्तु फिर भी इसकी कमी है।","विश्व में जल की कुल मात्रा लगातार कम होती जा रही है।"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q145","years":"2021","q_en":"Which of the following statements is true with regard to water on the global scale?","options_en":["There is not enough water available per capita.","We cannot reuse water.","There is a lot of water and yet there is scarcity.","The total amount of water in the world is constantly decreasing in quantity."]},{"id":"utet_2021_q146","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"प्रदूषण","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा ईंधन न्यूनतम पर्यावरणीय प्रदूषण उत्पन्न करता है?","options_hi":["डीजल","कोयला","हाइड्रोजन","केरोसिन"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q146","years":"2021","q_en":"Which one of the following fuels causes minimum environmental pollution?","options_en":["Diesel","Coal","Hydrogen","Kerosene"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q147","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र का अजैविक घटक है?","options_hi":["पौधे","कवक","ह्यूमस","बैक्टीरिया"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q147","years":"2021","q_en":"Which one of the following is an abiotic component of the ecosystem?","options_en":["Plants","Fungi","Humus","Bacteria"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q148","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"पारिस्थितिकी","q_hi":"मानव जब UV-किरणों से अत्यधिक प्रभावित हो जाते हैं तब क्या हो सकता है?\n(i) प्रतिरक्षा-तंत्र की क्षति (ii) फेफड़ों की क्षति (iii) त्वचा का कैंसर (iv) आमाशय के अल्सर","options_hi":["(i) और (ii)","(ii) और (iv)","(i) और (iii)","(iii) और (iv)"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2021 Q148","years":"2021","q_en":"Excessive exposure of humans to UV-rays results in —\n(i) damage to immune system (ii) damage to lungs (iii) skin cancer (iv) peptic ulcers","options_en":["(i) and (ii)","(ii) and (iv)","(i) and (iii)","(iii) and (iv)"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q149","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"प्रदूषण","q_hi":"फ्लोराइड प्रदूषण मुख्य रूप से प्रभावित करता है —","options_hi":["दाँत","हृदय","किडनी","मस्तिष्क"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2021 Q149","years":"2021","q_en":"Fluoride pollution mainly affects —","options_en":["Teeth","Heart","Kidney","Brain"]},{"id":"utet_2021_q150","exams":"utet1","section":"evs","topic":"प्रदूषण","q_hi":"आगरा में ताजमहल को अधिकतम प्रभावित करने वाले प्रदूषण का प्रकार है —","options_hi":["वायु प्रदूषण","जल प्रदूषण","मृदा प्रदूषण","शोर प्रदूषण"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2021 Q150","years":"2021","q_en":"The type of pollution which is likely to affect the Taj Mahal in Agra to a greater extent is —","options_en":["air pollution","water pollution","soil pollution","noise pollution"]}]''',
    '2022': r'''[{"id":"utet_2022_q1","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम की प्रकृति","q_hi":"किस विधि में व्यक्ति समस्या समाधान करने के लिए सभी विकल्पों को नहीं ढूँढता है अपितु केवल उन्हीं विकल्पों का चयन करता है और समस्या का समाधान करने की कोशिश करता है जो उसे संगत प्रतीत होते हैं।","options_hi":["स्वतः शोध अन्वेषण","यादृच्छिक अन्वेषण विधि","साधन-साध्य विश्लेषण","पश्चगामी अन्वेषण"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2022 Q1","years":"2022","q_en":"In which method, a person does not find all the options for problem solving but he only selects those options and tries to solve the problem which he finds appropriate.","options_en":["Heuristics","Random Search Method","Means-ends analysis","Backward search"]},{"id":"utet_2022_q2","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"भाषा विकास","q_hi":"कॉलम 'A' का मिलान कॉलम 'B' से कीजिए-\nकॉलम 'A': (1) ग्रामर (2) सीमैंटिक विकास (3) बेबलिंग (4) फोनोलॉजिकल विकास\nकॉलम 'B': (a) पहचानने योग्य भाषा बोलने की क्षमता (b) एक भाषा में निहित नियम (c) भाषा विकास की प्रारंभिक अवस्था (d) बोलने व लिखने की भाषा के अर्थ को समझना","options_hi":["(1-a)(2-b)(3-c)(4-d)","(1-b)(2-d)(3-c)(4-a)","(1-a)(2-c)(3-d)(4-b)","(1-c)(2-a)(3-d)(4-b)"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2022 Q2","years":"2022","q_en":"Match Column A with Column B — Column A: (1) Grammar (2) Semantic development (3) Babbling (4) Phonological development; Column B: (a) ability to produce recognizable speech (b) Rules within a given language (c) An early stage of speech development (d) Understanding of the meaning of spoken and written language","options_en":["(1-a)(2-b)(3-c)(4-d)","(1-b)(2-d)(3-c)(4-a)","(1-a)(2-c)(3-d)(4-b)","(1-c)(2-a)(3-d)(4-b)"]},{"id":"utet_2022_q3","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम सिद्धांत","q_hi":"शिक्षण अधिगम प्रक्रिया को प्रभावित करने वाले मनोवैज्ञानिक कारक हैं- (1) विद्यार्थियों में अभिप्रेरणा (2) सुंदर कक्षाकक्ष (3) रूचि एवं विद्यार्थियों में अभिक्षमता (4) विद्यालय की आधारभूत संरचना","options_hi":["1,2,3","1,2","1,3","3,4"],"ans":2,"source":"UTET 2022 Q3","years":"2022","q_en":"The psychological factors affecting the teaching learning process are - (1) Motivation of students (2) Beautiful classroom (3) Interest and aptitude of students (4) School infrastructure","options_en":["1,2,3","1,2","1,3","3,4"]},{"id":"utet_2022_q4","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम सिद्धांत","q_hi":"विशेष आवश्यकता वाले बच्चों के लिए शिक्षण अधिगम सामग्री होनी चाहिए","options_hi":["रंग बिरंगी","बहुसंवेदी","आकार में बड़ी","आकर्षक"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2022 Q4","years":"2022","q_en":"Teaching learning material for children with special needs should be","options_en":["Colourful","Multisensory","Big in size","Attractive"]},{"id":"utet_2022_q5","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"अधिगम की प्रकृति","q_hi":"जब एक विद्यार्थी उस व्यवहार को निष्पादित करना सीखता है जो सकारात्मक परिणाम देता है और उस व्यवहार को करने से बचता है जिससे उसे नकारात्मक परिणाम मिले, यह उदाहरण है","options_hi":["क्रिया प्रसूत अनुबंधन का","शास्त्रीय अनुबंधन का","समक्षणिक अनुबंधन का","संकेत कालिक अनुबंधन का"],"ans":0,"source":"UTET 2022 Q5","years":"2022","q_en":"When a student learns to perform behaviours that produce positive outcomes and to avoid behaviour that yields negative outcome, this is an example of","options_en":["Operant conditioning","Classical conditioning","Simultaneous conditioning","Trace conditioning"]},{"id":"utet_2022_q6","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"मूल्यांकन","q_hi":"आप किस परिस्थिति में विद्यार्थियों को सतत् पुनर्बलन देंगे","options_hi":["पूर्व व्यवहार को स्थापित करने के लिए","नए व्यवहार को स्थापित करने के लिए","नए व्यवहार को बनाए रखने के लिए","(B) और (C) दोनों"],"ans":1,"source":"UTET 2022 Q6","years":"2022","q_en":"In which situation will you give continuous reinforcement to students","options_en":["For establishing a past behaviour","For establishing a new behaviour","In maintaining a new behaviour","Both (B) and (C)"]},{"id":"utet_2022_q7","exams":"utet1","section":"cdp","topic":"स्मृति/सृजनात्मकता","q_hi":"यदि आपने कभी क